# =================================================== #
                PROBLEM DESCRITION
# =================================================== #


DataFrame report:

+-------------+--------+
| Column Name | Type   |
+-------------+--------+
| product     | object |
| quarter_1   | int    |
| quarter_2   | int    |
| quarter_3   | int    |
| quarter_4   | int    |
+-------------+--------+

Write a solution to reshape the data so that each row represents sales data for a product in a specific quarter.


# =================================================== #
                      SOLUTION
# =================================================== #


import pandas as pd

def meltTable(report: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:
    
    result = pd.melt(
        report,
        id_vars = ['product'],
        value_vars = [col for col in report.columns if col != 'product'],
        var_name = 'quarter',
        value_name = 'sales',
        ignore_index = True
    )

    return result 
